### Crypto Analysis Market Oracle API Tests
### 
### NOTE: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY must be configured in .env file (never in request body for security)
### All configuration fields in requests are optional - API key comes from .env
###
### NEW WORKFLOW (3 Steps):
### 1. Call /validate endpoint with YouTube URLs (returns analysis_id and validation results)
### 2. Call /analyze endpoint with analysis_id and economic calendar config
### 3. Call /process endpoint with analysis_id to get CSV data and full analysis
###
### EXPECTED RESPONSES:
### /validate returns: {"status": "success", "analysis_id": "20251220_152704", "transcripts": [...], ...}
### /analyze returns: {"status": "success", "analysis_id": "20251220_152704", "message": "..."}
### /process returns: {"status": "success", "csv_data": "...", "comprehensive_analysis": "...", ...}

### Variables
@baseUrl = http://localhost:5000
@analysisId = 20251220_171719
### ^ Update this variable with the analysis_id from /validate response
### Example: If /validate returns "analysis_id": "20251220_152704", update @analysisId = 20251220_152704

### 1. Get App Status (Root Endpoint)
GET {{baseUrl}}/
Content-Type: application/json

###

### ============================================================================
### STEP 1: VALIDATE YOUTUBE TRANSCRIPTS (Returns analysis_id)
### ============================================================================

### 1. Validate YouTube URLs - Single URL
### This is the FIRST endpoint to call. It validates YouTube URLs, extracts transcripts,
### creates an analysis directory, and returns validation results with analysis_id.
### 
### Response example:
### {
###   "status": "success",
###   "analysis_id": "20251220_152704",
###   "transcripts": [
###     {
###       "url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=bgV5FnP8gpA",
###       "success": true,
###       "video_id": "bgV5FnP8gpA",
###       "error": null
###     }
###   ],
###   "summary": {
###     "total": 1,
###     "successful": 1,
###     "failed": 0
###   },
###   "message": "Validation completed. 1/1 transcripts extracted successfully. Use analysis_id in /analyze endpoint."
### }
### 
### IMPORTANT: Copy the "analysis_id" value and use it in the /analyze endpoint!
POST {{baseUrl}}/validate
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "youtube_urls": [
    "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=bgV5FnP8gpA"
  ]
}

###

### 2. Validate YouTube URLs - Multiple URLs
### Check which URLs succeeded and which failed before proceeding
POST {{baseUrl}}/validate
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "youtube_urls": [
    "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=bgV5FnP8gpA",
    "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=FZyVMrIZ26Q",
    "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OMe51EPE844",
    "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=nwhBTCeeT7Y",
    "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Dcw-A0iZjuc",
    "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9zgnpjM3J1I",
    "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-m-2wAhiB1k"
  ]
}

###

### 3. Validate YouTube URLs - Error Test (Missing youtube_urls)
POST {{baseUrl}}/validate
Content-Type: application/json

{}

###

### 4. Validate YouTube URLs - Error Test (Invalid URL)
POST {{baseUrl}}/validate
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "youtube_urls": [
    "https://invalid-url.com"
  ]
}

###

### ============================================================================
### STEP 2: RUN ANALYSIS (Requires analysis_id from /validate)
### ============================================================================

### 5. Run Analysis - Minimal (Only analysis_id, uses defaults from .env)
### NOTE: This endpoint requires analysis_id from /validate endpoint.
### It does NOT take youtube_urls anymore - those are handled by /validate.
### 
### Response example:
### {
###   "status": "success",
###   "analysis_id": "20251220_152704",
###   "message": "Analysis completed. Use /process endpoint with analysis_id: 20251220_152704 to generate CSV data."
### }
POST {{baseUrl}}/analyze
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "analysis_id": "{{analysisId}}"
}

###

### 6. Run Analysis - With ForexFactory Configuration
POST {{baseUrl}}/analyze
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "analysis_id": "{{analysisId}}",
  "forexfactory_start_date": "2025-12-14",
  "forexfactory_use_week": true
}

###

### 7. Run Analysis - With TradingEconomics Configuration
POST {{baseUrl}}/analyze
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "analysis_id": "{{analysisId}}",
  "tradingeconomics_start_date": "2025-12-15",
  "tradingeconomics_end_date": "2025-12-21"
}

###

### 8. Run Analysis - Full Configuration
POST {{baseUrl}}/analyze
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "analysis_id": "{{analysisId}}",
  "forexfactory_start_date": "2025-12-14",
  "forexfactory_use_week": true,
  "tradingeconomics_start_date": "2025-12-15",
  "tradingeconomics_end_date": "2025-12-21"
}

###

### 9. Run Analysis - Error Test (Missing analysis_id)
POST {{baseUrl}}/analyze
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "forexfactory_start_date": "2025-12-14"
}

###

### 10. Run Analysis - Error Test (Invalid analysis_id)
POST {{baseUrl}}/analyze
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "analysis_id": "invalid_id_12345",
  "forexfactory_start_date": "2025-12-14"
}

###


###

### 11. Run Analysis - Error Test (Invalid Date Format)
POST {{baseUrl}}/analyze
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "analysis_id": "{{analysisId}}",
  "forexfactory_start_date": "invalid-date-format"
}

###

### ============================================================================
### STEP 3: PROCESS ANALYSIS (Generate CSV from analysis_id)
### ============================================================================

### 12. Process Analysis - Generate CSV (Using Variable)
### IMPORTANT: Update @analysisId variable at the top of this file with the analysis_id from /analyze response
### This endpoint will:
### - Read comprehensive_analysis.txt from the analysis directory
### - Generate CSV data using Anthropic AI (extracts events, prices, predictions)
### - Return both CSV data and full comprehensive analysis
###
### Response example:
### {
###   "status": "success",
###   "analysis_directory": "analysis\\20251220_152704",
###   "csv_data": "Token,Date,Event_Type,Event_Category,Price_Level,Price_Type,Pattern,Timeframe,Event_Description,Content_Source,Confidence_Level\n...",
###   "comprehensive_analysis": "# Full Comprehensive Events Analysis\n\nGenerated: 2025-12-20T04:17:32...",
###   "forexfactory_events_count": 130,
###   "tradingeconomics_events_count": 65,
###   "youtube_transcripts_count": 7,
###   "message": "Processing completed successfully"
### }
POST {{baseUrl}}/process
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "analysis_id": "{{analysisId}}"
}

###

### 13. Process Analysis - Direct ID (Replace with actual analysis_id)
### Use this if you want to test with a specific analysis_id without updating the variable
POST {{baseUrl}}/process
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "analysis_id": "20251220_152704"
}

###

### 14. Process Analysis - Error Test - Missing analysis_id
POST {{baseUrl}}/process
Content-Type: application/json

{}

###

### 15. Process Analysis - Error Test - Invalid analysis_id
POST {{baseUrl}}/process
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "analysis_id": "invalid_id_12345"
}

###

### ============================================================================
### COMPLETE WORKFLOW EXAMPLE
### ============================================================================

### 16. Complete Workflow: Step 1 - Validate YouTube URLs
### Copy the "analysis_id" from the response
POST {{baseUrl}}/validate
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "youtube_urls": [
    "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=bgV5FnP8gpA",
    "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=FZyVMrIZ26Q"
  ]
}

###

### 17. Complete Workflow: Step 2 - Run Analysis
### Use the analysis_id from Step 1 (e.g., "20251220_152704")
POST {{baseUrl}}/analyze
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "analysis_id": "20251220_152704",
  "forexfactory_start_date": "2025-12-14",
  "forexfactory_use_week": true,
  "tradingeconomics_start_date": "2025-12-15",
  "tradingeconomics_end_date": "2025-12-21"
}

###

### 18. Complete Workflow: Step 3 - Process Analysis
### Use the analysis_id from Step 1 response (e.g., "20251220_152704")
### Replace "20251220_152704" with the actual analysis_id from Step 1
### 
### This will return:
### - csv_data: CSV formatted data with all events, prices, predictions
###   * Event_Type: "Listed" (ForexFactory/TradingEconomics), "Mentioned" (transcripts), "Predicted" (AI forecasts)
###   * Event_Category: Price Movement, Support Level, Economic Data, etc.
###   * All price levels, dates, and predictions extracted from the analysis
### - comprehensive_analysis: Full analysis text (complete file content)
### - Event counts and metadata
POST {{baseUrl}}/process
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "analysis_id": "20251220_152704"
}

###

