### 22. Test: Process and Verify CSV Structure
### After running this, check that csv_data contains:
### - Header row with 12 columns
### - Event_Type values are only: "Listed", "Mentioned", or "Predicted"
### - Dates in YYYY-MM-DD format
### - Price_Level values have $ symbol
POST {{baseUrl}}/process
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "analysis_id": "{{analysisId}}"
}

###

### ============================================================================
### CSV DATA STRUCTURE REFERENCE
### ============================================================================
###
### The CSV data returned by /process endpoint has the following structure:
###
### Columns (12 total):
### 1. Token - Cryptocurrency (Bitcoin, Ethereum, XRP, Crypto, General)
### 2. Date - Event date (YYYY-MM-DD format)
### 3. Event_Type - MUST be one of:
###    * "Listed" - Real-world events from ForexFactory/TradingEconomics
###    * "Mentioned" - Events/dates from YouTube transcripts or analyst discussions
###    * "Predicted" - AI-generated predictions, forecasts, scenarios
### 4. Event_Category - Type of event:
###    * Price Movement, Regulatory, Market Pattern, Support Level, 
###      Resistance Level, Rate Decision, Economic Data, Astronomical, etc.
### 5. Price_Level - Price points with $ symbol (e.g., "$50000", "$1.75") or "N/A"
### 6. Price_Type - Support, Resistance, Target, Current, Peak, Bottom, Breakout, or "N/A"
### 7. Pattern - Chart patterns or market structures, or "N/A"
### 8. Timeframe - Past, Present, or Future
### 9. Event_Description - Detailed description of the event/prediction
### 10. Content_Source - ForexFactory, TradingEconomics, YouTube Transcript, Multiple, or Analysis
### 11. Confidence_Level - High, Medium, Low, probability %, or "N/A"
###
### Example CSV row:
### Bitcoin,2025-12-19,Listed,Economic Data,N/A,N/A,N/A,Future,UK Retail Sales - Strong retail sales = hawkish BOE concerns,ForexFactory,N/A
###
### ============================================================================

